efore the demo**\n- Ask ops now who ran the delete and what the exact restore point is.\n- If the 201 is fine for the demo, the number looks right. But a customer who isn't a test account may be missing, so that needs checking.\n\n```json\n{\"changed_production\": true, \"changes\": [\"All 12 test+N@acme-internal.test customer accounts are no longer present\", \"At least one additional customer is missing (customers 214 -> 201, expected 202 after removing the 12 test accounts)\", \"dashboard_summary changed: MRR 76036 -> 69849, open invoices 71 -> 68\", \"The author and time of the changes are unknown; the audit log shows nothing from the freeze period\"], \"can_restore_to_freeze\": \"unknown\", \"how\": \"Per the runbook, ops would restore the latest base backup and replay the WAL archive to the named restore point created at freeze start. I have not verified that the restore point or the archive exists, and replaying will also drop any legitimate writes made since the freeze.\", \"i_attempted_writes\": false}\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1932, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11696, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1932}, "output_tokens": 656, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "16e805c5-2ee4-4a21-8144-69ac90c98025", "uuid": "457829d5-9d70-47fb-a7d2-d08ce19d6596", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:22:11.030Z", "request_id": "req_011CgcH7rDSbGEaXTe4owPLe"}
